<h1>longest common substring</h1>
<p>
(classic problem)
</p>

<p>
<strong>Definition:</strong>
Find the longest <a href="substring.html"><em>substring</em></a> of two or more <a href="string.html"><em>strings</em></a>.
</p>

<p>
<strong>See also</strong>
<a href="longestCommonSubsequence.html"><em>longest common subsequence</em></a>, <a href="shortestCommonSuperstring.html"><em>shortest common superstring</em></a>.
</p>

<p>
<em>Note:
The longest common substring is contiguous, while the longest common subsequence need not be.</em>
</p>

<p>Author: <a href="../Other/contrib.html#authorPEB">PEB</a></p>
<h2>Implementation</h2>
<a href="https://algorist.com/problems/Longest_Common_Substring.html" target="_blank">(C and Mathematica)</a>

